            <ArticleTitle>Femoral endarteritis as a complication of percutaneous coronary intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Infectious complications following percutaneous coronary interventions are extremely unusual, with a reported frequency of less than 1%. This report describes a patient who developed septic endarteritis as a complication of percutaneous coronary intervention and reviews the literature of this complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
